# Output SOP (P0) — structured, human + machine readable

Binds **every** agent, subagent, fleet worker, and orchestrator turn. Not a style preference.
Breaking it means the operator does not review the output, so the work does not land.

## The rule

**Default to structured. Prose is the exception, never the container.**

| Content | Required form |
|---|---|
| Any status, inventory, comparison, or result set | **table** |
| Config, manifest, contract, schema, payload | **fenced YAML or JSON** |
| Sequence / dependency / state machine / flow | **mermaid diagram** |
| Numeric series, distribution, trend | **chart** (mermaid, or an artifact when richer) |
| Per-item verdicts (pass/fail/blocked) | **table with an explicit status column** |
| Rationale for a decision | ≤2 sentences, attached to the row it explains |

**Scope: GLOBAL.** Binds every repo, project, session and machine — not one repo. This file is the
canonical rule; `just cursor-setup` links it into `~/.cursor/rules`. Repo-level `CLAUDE.md` and
`AGENTS.md` files point here, never restate.

## Links are mandatory, not decorative

Every referenced artifact appears as a **resolvable link in the cell that names it** — never a
bare number or name the reader has to go find.

| Artifact | Required form |
|---|---|
| Issue tracker issue | issue key linked to its URL — `[ABC-123](<issue-url>)` |
| Issue tracker project / epic | full project URL |
| PR | `[org/repo#92](https://github.com/org/repo/pull/92)` — org/repo prefixed when >1 repo is in scope |
| Commit / branch | short SHA linked to the commit; branch name verbatim |
| Build / CI run | build or run ID + link to it |
| Image | `repo/name@sha256:<12-hex min>` — digest, never a floating tag |
| Doc / playbook / draft | repo-relative path |
| Cluster / node pool / object store | fully qualified name (`project/cluster/pool`, `bucket/prefix`) |

A row that cites a PR, issue, build or digest without its link is incomplete — same defect class
as a missing version tuple. When a report is posted **into** an issue tracker or a PR, cross-link
the other direction too, so the artifact and the tracker each point at the other.

## Hard requirements

1. **Every row carries its full identifying tuple.** Versions, digests, branch/commit SHAs, PR
   numbers, build IDs. A row missing them is a defect in the report, not a formatting nit.
2. **Never bury a number, verdict, or identifier in a sentence.** If it is data, it goes in a cell.
3. **Status columns use fixed vocabulary**, not adjectives: `PASS | FAIL | BLOCKED | PENDING |
   SKIPPED | UNKNOWN`. `UNKNOWN` is mandatory when something was not measured — never infer.
4. **Verified vs inferred is a column**, not a caveat buried in prose.
5. **Machine-readable summary block** on any report another agent or tool will consume — fenced
   YAML/JSON, so it can be parsed without an LLM.
6. **Prose budget: ≤2 sentences per point.** Analysis lives in the table; the sentence explains
   *why*, never *what*.

## Canonical shapes

Per-item status:

```
| Item | Version tuple / digest | Status | Evidence ref | Verified? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| service-a | py3.13.2 / libfoo1.4.0 / sha256:9f21… | PASS | <evidence-uri> | measured |
| service-b | py3.13.2 / libfoo1.3.7 / sha256:0ab4… | UNKNOWN | — | not measured |
```

Machine-readable tail on any consumable report:

```yaml
summary:
  lane: <name>
  status: PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED
  blockers: [<id>, …]
  next_action: <one line>
  evidence: [<uri>, …]
```

Dependency / land order:

```mermaid
graph LR
  A[#83 MERGED] --> B[#86 CI]
  B --> C[#91 retarget]
```

## Enforcement

- Referenced as **P0 from `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`** — every session loads it.
- Every spawned agent's prompt MUST carry the reporting fragment below, verbatim, alongside the
  permission/verification fragments. Omitting it is a designer failure, same class as a permission
  gap.

### Mandatory agent prompt fragment

```
REPORTING (P0 — SOP, not preference)
Report in structured form: tables for any status/inventory/comparison/result set, fenced
YAML/JSON for config/contracts/payloads, mermaid for sequences and dependency graphs, charts
for numeric series. Every row carries its full version tuple and digest/SHA. Status columns use
PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED|PENDING|SKIPPED|UNKNOWN — never adjectives, and UNKNOWN where you did not
measure. Add a "verified vs inferred" column. End any report another agent will consume with a
fenced YAML `summary:` block (lane, status, blockers, next_action, evidence). Prose <= 2
sentences per point, attached to the row it explains. Never bury a number, verdict, digest or
identifier in a sentence.
```

